    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "The student works backwards from the curved surface area of a cylinder to find h. The task supplies the substitution frame, with the radius, the simplified 10πh and the final division to fill in. The decisions are limited to reading r from the diagram, recalling that curved area is 2πrh, and dividing through by 10π, which cancels π cleanly. That is more than the direct labelling and area calculation in p20-q1. It is less than p22-q7, where the student must link circumference, radius and sector area. It is also clearly easier than the unscaffolded p22-q8, which needs a decimal rounding step.",
